From d48a551dc8caa0f722b6a1adcfa702a4b7e2babc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 13:50:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 006/638] mojo: define the AROS bootstrap transport boundary
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-bringup

AI_STATUS: wip

ROOT_CAUSE: Mojo's POSIX platform channel assumes AF_UNIX socketpairs and transferable file descriptors; wrapping an AROSTCP socket or integer placeholder would compile but misrepresent ownership and cross-process semantics.

FIX_REASON: Select explicit AROS channel stubs for the initial single-process headless graph, return unsupported at cross-process bootstrap points, preserve 64-bit task identity without narrowing it onto Mojo's compatibility wire field, and emit the boundary through AROS debug output.

SCOPE: Mojo platform-channel source selection, named/server/socket utility stubs, platform_channel construction, and node process-identity compatibility.

VALIDATION: focused platform-channel and node-channel objects compile; headless_shell generation no longer imports AF_UNIX implementations on AROS.

RISK: high for multiprocess Chromium; native Exec message-port/OPAL channel transport is required before renderer or GPU process isolation is enabled.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
